{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790286412,"nonce":"Him4MKBdl8PLqtM3V57cMq78+8s=","title":"Macro Expr values cover only EConst/ECall/EField; typed-expression API and constant macro params missing","message":"A macro could take apart and rebuild only EConst, ECall and EField. Every other ExprDef read as an opaque Expr and could not be built: ESwitch was an undefined variable (Issue7359). EBinop's operator was a debug string rather than a Binop, and EMeta names dropped the colon (`@:foo` read as \"foo\").\n\nOther gaps:\n- `Context.typeExpr(e).expr` had no TField shape, so Issue4126 and Issue7007 failed. `storeTypedExpr`/`getTypedExpr` could not hand back the source expression.\n- A caught compiler error was not a `haxe.macro.Error`.\n- A bare constructor name in a pattern (`OpAdd`, `FArrow`) bound as a capture and matched anything.\n- A macro parameter declared `a:String` / `b:Array\u003cString\u003e` / `c:{}` received the Expr, where Haxe passes the constant. A single-quoted string arrives as its raw text (Issue1284).\n- `macro a =\u003e b` failed to parse (Issue6531).\n\nFix: expr_adt.rs maps every ExprDef, Constant, Binop/Unop, FunctionKind and ComplexType both ways, with case patterns as expressions. The interpreter builds every constructor. MacroDefinition records which parameters take constants.\n\nConformance 653 -\u003e 658 (Issue1284, 2558, 4126, 7007, 7359), 0 LOST. MOVED: Issue6531 is now blocked on Printer.printExpr failing to compile (\"Captured value not found in value_map\"); Issue10744 moved from the earlier parser commit. Still open: Issue6830 needs a typedef's @:const type argument kept through Context.typeof; Issue3914 crashes when a stored typed lambda is re-lowered at another site.","files":null}]}